3. Public-Source Requirement

Any Use of the Software must remain open and public-source.

If You modify, extend, integrate, deploy, distribute, publish, or publicly
present any work that uses or depends on the Software, You must:

- make Your complete corresponding source code and Modifications publicly
  available at no charge;
- include the scripts, configs, prompts, training recipes, evaluation commands,
  and documentation reasonably needed to reproduce Your changes and results;
- keep this license and copyright notice with the Software and any
  Modifications;
- clearly state what You changed; and
- link back to the original AlphaHand repository or project page.

You may not use the Software in a closed-source project, closed-source model
pipeline, closed-source dataset pipeline, closed-source product, or private
deployment unless the Licensor gives You separate written permission.

